Pontypridd sits where the Rhondda meets the Taff, with the A470 running south to Cardiff and north to Merthyr Tydfil. Shops in town, firms on Treforest Industrial Estate, and businesses in Church Village, Llantrisant and Tonyrefail all get enquiries from people who searched before they visited. If that search does not find you, it finds someone else.

NC Digital builds WordPress websites for those businesses. We are based in Merthyr Tydfil. We do not have an office in Pontypridd. The build is done remotely, and we can meet in person in the valley when a face-to-face conversation is useful.

## Affordable web design in Pontypridd

Published starting prices, so you can budget before a call:

- **One-page WordPress website:** from £199
- **Multi-page WordPress website:** from £600
- **Ecommerce website:** from £800
- **Pay-monthly website:** from £20 a month

All prices include VAT. A one-page site suits a business with one main service. A multi-page site suits several services or several towns, because each page can answer one search. An online shop is a separate job. The pay-monthly option is a managed site with the domain and hosting included and no upfront cost.

The detail of what changes the price is in [how much web design costs in Cardiff](/blog/how-much-does-web-design-cost-in-cardiff/). For a rough figure, use the [website cost calculator](/website-cost-calculator/). The service itself is described on our [web design](/services/web-design/) page, and the same starting prices are on [web design Cardiff](/web-design-cardiff/).

## The towns this page is for

Pontypridd town centre is the obvious one, but the searches we plan for are wider than the high street.

- **Treforest, Glyntaff and Rhydyfelin** sit on the edge of town, with Treforest Industrial Estate and the university campus bringing a mix of employers, suppliers and student-facing businesses.
- **Hawthorn, Trallwn and Ynysybwl** are close enough that customers often treat them as the same local search.
- **Church Village, Llantwit Fardre and Beddau** look south towards Cardiff as well as back towards Pontypridd.
- **Llantrisant, Talbot Green and Tonyrefail** have their own shops and trades, and people there still search “near Pontypridd”.
- **Abercynon** sits up the Taff, between Pontypridd and Merthyr.

A website for this area should name the places you actually cover. A plumber in Church Village and a fabricator on the industrial estate do not need the same pages. We plan the pages around your services and the towns you will travel to, then write them so they are not a copy of a Cardiff or Aberdare page with the town name swapped.

## How a Pontypridd project runs

You deal with Nathan, the developer who builds the site. There is no Pontypridd office and no account handler in between.

1. Tell us what you do, which towns you cover, and whether you need one page, several pages, or a shop.
2. We agree the pages, the price and what you need to send: words, logo and photos.
3. The site is built in WordPress. You review it before it goes live.
4. We show you how to edit it. Hosting with SSL is available if you want us to look after that too.

Most straightforward sites are finished within 7–14 days of us having the content. Larger sites take longer when there are more pages. Meetings can be a video call or in person. The build itself does not depend on you coming to Merthyr or us sitting in your premises.

